2. Encodings derived from hardware documentation
------------------------------------------------

The QPU instruction encoder and disassembler (infer/tools/qenc.py,
infer/tools/kgen.py, tools/qpu_disasm.py) and the field tables in
infer/tools/vpmwords.py are written out from the Broadcom VideoCore IV 3D
Architecture Reference Guide (AG100-R) and from the Broadcom-copyright
register/opcode definitions published in:

    anholt/vc4-gpu-tools             https://github.com/anholt/vc4-gpu-tools
        vc4_qpu_defines.h, vc4_packet.h, vc4_qpu_disasm.c (MIT)
    hermanhermitage/videocoreiv-qpu  https://github.com/hermanhermitage/videocoreiv-qpu

No header from those trees is copied verbatim; the enums and field maps are
re-expressed in Python and C.

